    Bug 1806770 - Remove IMAP UID functions in DB for now to avoid confusion. r=mkmelin


    A while back I added some IMAP UID functions to the database/msghdr interfaces to prepare for storing IMAP UIDs separately from nsMsgKeys.
    As we get closer to performing the separation, these functions have the potential to be confusing.
    To ease the separation, I'm consolidating UID<->nsMsgKey mappings into a smaller number of helper functions, and the
    current implementation of these helper functions just cast directly between ImapUid and nsMsgKey, which is what the current code expects.
    But having both these and the real UID functions in the database (ie complete independent storage from nsMsgKey) has the potential to be very confusing.
    So this patch removes them all the real UID functions for now.
    We'll back out this patch to restore the real UID functions when need them.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D307676

